{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-10564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cot}^{2}⁡x & ={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2({csc}^{2}⁡x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{csc}^{2}⁡x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{x}{2}+2{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-10564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0f6f97bc9e50734f63fa091b4cb3bda2181f63c544cca431bccc82929c0c415"} {"question" "q-10564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-10564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{4}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-10564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡x-{x}^{2}{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}({x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡x-{x}^{2}{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{2}({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{3}-{0}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0f6f97bc9e50734f63fa091b4cb3bda2181f63c544cca431bccc82929c0c415"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-1"] ["math" "{\\pi }^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-73525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sin}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0f6f97bc9e50734f63fa091b4cb3bda2181f63c544cca431bccc82929c0c415"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}-1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-114460" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-352671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-352671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the secant-tangent identity:\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6\\cdot 1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{6}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =6[\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =6(1-0) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-352671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0f6f97bc9e50734f63fa091b4cb3bda2181f63c544cca431bccc82929c0c415"} {"question" "q-352671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-352671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-362813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-3{x}^{2}{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-362813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the identity ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-3{x}^{2}{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}[{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{cot}^{2}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & ={1}^{3}-{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-362813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c0f6f97bc9e50734f63fa091b4cb3bda2181f63c544cca431bccc82929c0c415"} {"question" "q-362813" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"} {"question" "q-362813" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066499/state.json" "file_sha256" "89164833a8906af1380331f35723139d0ea6abd3b02a4b305dfabf82dcc6a9a8"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2200 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
